==English==

===Etymology===
Originally meant "bull's penis" (originally described as "bull's prick"). Whether it was ever applied to other animals or humans is unknown - but as "wazz" is used for human urination in the West and North of England, so this maybe true. Contrary to the afore mentioned it may also originate from the word 'wiseacher' meaning someone who plays the fool without knowing it. However as this is an American slang, and Wazzock is an English slang term, this may not be true.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|UK|mildly|pejorative}} {{slang}} a [[stupid]] or [[annoying]] person.

